authored_scope:
Random mode builds a latent board with 2..6 holes. Holes are 4-connected polyominoes of 1..7 cells that do not enclose board cells, stay off the board rim and are mutually 8-separated. Every scene has at least two shape classes and at least one non-monomino hole, and same-size competitor holes are biased in. Each piece is a random rotation or reflection of its hole, scaled by k=2 or 3 (k=4 on request), and placed with 8-separated bounding boxes. Noise is single dots plus optional dominoes or trominoes; it may sit inside a concave piece's box, as in the test, but never touches a piece or the board box. Grid sizes are 10..30 (12..30 by default). Sizes beyond the fixtures, and k=4, are synthetic extensions. Not supported:
- a non-zero background;
- holes touching the board rim;
- holes enclosing board islands;
- multiple boards;
- pieces whose boxes interleave;
- noise inside the board box.
